                              <div type="background">    	
                                        <head>Background</head>
                              	<p>This is an edition by Anna C. Horn and Robert K. Paulsen of <title>Landslọg Magnúss Hákonarsonar</title> (<title>Magnus Lagabøtes Landslov</title>) in the manuscript Holm perg 34 4to, fols. 8r–75r (c. 1275–1300). It is a digitally-born edition, transcribed directly from photographic facsimiles of the manuscript. The text is displayed on three levels, the facsimile level [facs], the diplomatic level [dipl] and the normalised level [norm]. The normalised orthography follows that of the <title>Ordbog  over det norrøne prosasprog</title> (ONP), as discussed in ch. 10 of the Menota Handbook.</p>
                                        <p>All pages of the manuscript can be displayed in photographic facsimiles in full colour, and each page may be copied directly from the web page for a closer study. The photographs have been delivered by The Royal Library (Kungliga biblioteket) in Stockholm, where the manuscript is housed.</p>
                                        <p>This edition offers a full morphological annotation, including the lemma (in the orthography of ONP) and the grammatical form for each word. This annotation will be shown when selecting and clicking on a word in the text, and it is also accessible by the search facilities in Menota. Here, the text may be searched alongside a number of other annotated texts in the archive. For the latter, see the <hi rend="bold">Documentation</hi> in the column to the left and its <hi rend="bold">Helpdesk</hi> link.</p>
                                        <p>Furthermore, the text is supplied by a parallel translation into Modern Norwegian. This translation has been made by Anna C. Horn, and will be  discussed in the ensuing introduction.</p>
                                        <p>At a later stage, this edition will be supplemented by the syntactic annotation of the manuscript from the Menotec project.</p>
                              </div>
